  "desks": [
    {
      "title": "Series A diligence — Tidewell (climate logistics)",
      "description": "Thirteen diligence workstreams ahead of investment committee: what has to be true, what the customer calls said, and the one number that decides the recommendation.",
      "dueInDays": 6,
      "brief": "## Series A diligence — Tidewell\n\n**What they do** emissions tracking and route optimisation for mid-sized road freight carriers\n**Round** $10M Series A at $30M pre ($40M post) · **We'd lead** $6M for 15%\n**Deal team** Amara (partner), Joon, Felix · **Investment committee** @+6d\n\n### Thesis in one line\nCarriers running 50–500 trucks will need audited emissions data to keep their enterprise shippers, and Tidewell is the cheapest way to get it — with fuel savings that pay for the software.\n\n### What has to be true\n- Net revenue retention stays above 120% as cohorts age\n- Gross margin per carrier reaches 60% once onboarding is productised\n- The emissions methodology survives a shipper's auditor, with diesel factors that reconcile to the NGER Measurement Determination\n\n### Where it stands\nSeven of thirteen workstreams done. Team and commercial look strong. **Unit economics is the open question:** margin per carrier is 41% today, and the committee will ask why that changes.",
      "callout": {
        "title": "Swing factor: margin per carrier",
        "body": "41% today against 60% in the plan. If the self-serve telematics connector cuts onboarding from three weeks to one, the model gets there by month 18. Joon has the test data @+2d — that answer decides the recommendation.",
        "accent": "#ef4444",
        "icon": "🔍"
      },
